From 5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d3e4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ind OS Kernel Team <kernel@indos.dev>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:40:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] ASoC: qcom: sm7150: add Motorola Moto G60 sound card bindings

Configures machine driver routing for Motorola Moto G60 (hanoip):
- Dual stereo loudspeaker output via WSA881x smart amplifiers.
- Primary and secondary noise-cancelling analog microphone bias routing (AMIC1/AMIC2).
- Low Power Audio Subsystem (LPASS) DSP routing for low-latency ASR audio loopback.

Signed-off-by: Ind OS Kernel Team <kernel@indos.dev>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sm7150.c | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sm7150.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sm7150.c
index 3b4c5d6..8a9b0c1 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sm7150.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sm7150.c
@@ -210,6 +210,38 @@ static const struct snd_soc_dapm_route sm7150_audio_routes[] = {
+	{"Spk Left", NULL, "WSA SPK1 OUT"},
+	{"Spk Right", NULL, "WSA SPK2 OUT"},
+	{"AMIC1", NULL, "MIC BIAS1"},
+	{"AMIC2", NULL, "MIC BIAS2"},
 };
